# 17. Random Forest vs Gradient Boosting

This is a common interview comparison.

## Random Forest

Trees are generally built independently.

```text
Tree 1 ─┐
Tree 2 ─┼──→ Combine
Tree 3 ─┘
```

This is primarily:

> **Bagging**

---

## Gradient Boosting

Trees are built sequentially.

```text
Tree 1
   ↓
Correct Errors
   ↓
Tree 2
   ↓
Correct Remaining Errors
   ↓
Tree 3
```

This is:

> **Boosting**

🔥 Remember:

```text
Random Forest → Parallel-style independent trees → Bagging

Gradient Boosting → Sequential error correction → Boosting
```

