# 25. Explain to an Interviewer — 60-Second Script 🎤

> Random Forest is an ensemble learning algorithm that combines multiple Decision Trees to produce a more robust prediction. Each tree is trained using a bootstrap sample of the training data, and at each split it considers a random subset of features. These mechanisms reduce correlation between trees and help reduce the variance associated with a single Decision Tree. For classification, the forest usually aggregates predictions using majority voting, while for regression it averages predictions. Random Forest is effective for nonlinear relationships and tabular data, although it requires more computation and is less interpretable than a single tree.

